msgstr "NONE and PRIMASK require a zero syscall ceiling. BASEPRI requires a nonzero unshifted ceiling. Configuration owns these facts; a wake target cannot weaken them."

msgid "Success establishes nominal hardware programming, not a guaranteed deadline. Both timeout bounds remain zero when oscillator limits are unknown. A product requiring bounded timing must admit the oscillator profile before activation. Enable runs in a privileged task and is serialized with feed, state and platform stop. Install IRQ feeding only after this call returns; activation does not support a concurrent reload during shadow-register programming."
msgstr "Success establishes nominal hardware programming, not a guaranteed deadline. Both timeout bounds remain zero when oscillator limits are unknown. A product requiring bounded timing must admit the oscillator profile before activation. Enable runs in a privileged task and is serialized with feed, state and platform stop. Install IRQ feeding only after this call returns; activation does not support a concurrent reload during shadow-register programming."

msgid "[inout] Fixed provider; product owns feed/recovery policy."
msgstr "[inout] Fixed provider; product owns feed/recovery policy."

msgid "[in] Requested nominal timeout in maintained range."
msgstr "[in] Requested nominal timeout in maintained range."

msgid "[in] Whether debug halting freezes counting."
msgstr "[in] Whether debug halting freezes counting."

msgid "[out] Actual timeout bounds and remaining effect, including enabled=true when later setup reports failure after enabling."
msgstr "[out] Actual timeout bounds and remaining effect, including enabled=true when later setup reports failure after enabling."

msgid "Success or INVALID/STATE/IO; never claims enabled hardware was disabled during rollback. Existing enable is identified."
msgstr "Success or INVALID/STATE/IO; never claims enabled hardware was disabled during rollback. Existing enable is identified."

msgid "[inout] Fixed enabled provider with one serialized feed owner."
msgstr "[inout] Fixed enabled provider with one serialized feed owner."

msgid "Success or INVALID/STATE; bounded task/IRQ, no allocation."
msgstr "Success or INVALID/STATE; bounded task/IRQ, no allocation."

msgid "[in] Fixed provider."
msgstr "[in] Fixed provider."

msgid "[out] Current hardware/remembered initialization state."
msgstr "[out] Current hardware/remembered initialization state."

msgid "Success or INVALID; UNSUPPORTED retains observed hardware effects with both timeout bounds zero when those bounds cannot be established. Never infer a disabled watchdog from a failed query or unknown timeout."
msgstr "Success or INVALID; UNSUPPORTED retains observed hardware effects with both timeout bounds zero when those bounds cannot be established. Never infer a disabled watchdog from a failed query or unknown timeout."

msgid "No implicit acknowledgement, reboot or product classification."
msgstr "No implicit acknowledgement, reboot or product classification."

msgid "Bitmask of NX_RESET_*; multiple causes may be reported."
msgstr "Bitmask of NX_RESET_*; multiple causes may be reported."

msgid "A zero minimum and maximum mean the timeout bounds are unknown, for example while hardware shadow updates remain pending or no oscillator limits have been reviewed. The enabled, irreversible and debug_freeze facts remain valid."
msgstr "A zero minimum and maximum mean the timeout bounds are unknown, for example while hardware shadow updates remain pending or no oscillator limits have been reviewed. The enabled, irreversible and debug_freeze facts remain valid."

msgid "required = targets + spares + ceil(rate*release_delay / (block_units*1000000)); payload is required*block*unit_bytes. Finite math is conservative under the declared FIFO frontier release bound; out-of-order release may still block the next cursor. Latency requires target_delay_us < floor(units_per_block*1000000/units_per_second). This creates no backpressure or hardware qualification."
msgstr "required = targets + spares + ceil(rate*release_delay / (block_units*1000000)); payload is required*block*unit_bytes. Finite math is conservative under the declared FIFO frontier release bound; out-of-order release may still block the next cursor. Latency requires target_delay_us < floor(units_per_block*1000000/units_per_second). This creates no backpressure or hardware qualification."
